    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162-a4">

                <pb facs="0581" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg459"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 68.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Circular to Canadian collectors of
                    customs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Customs Department</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1889-06-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 1,
                    1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">memorandum.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Collector of Customs</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Port of</hi>——.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">“Shipping master’s certificate.”</p>
                <p>The undersigned is instructed by the minister of customs to call your attention
                    to section 32, chapter 74, Revised Statutes of Canada, 1886, and to inform you
                    that he is advised that the provisions of said section apply to foreign vessels,
                    including, of course, vessels of the United States, and you should, therefore,
                    refuse clearance in all cases until “the shipping master’s certificate to the
                    effect that all requirements <pb facs="0582" n="460" xml:id="pg460"/> of this
                    act have been complied with, or to the effect that the agreement is in his
                    office partially signed, waiting an engagement of a portion of the crew, as the
                    case may be,” has been produced by the master or proper officer of the ship.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Johnson</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Commissioner.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
